{
  "id": 1997,
  "title": "First Day Where You Have Been in All the Rooms",
  "slug": "first-day-where-you-have-been-in-all-the-rooms",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "topics": [
    "Array",
    "Dynamic Programming"
  ],
  "description": "There are n rooms you need to visit, labeled from 0 to n - 1. Each day is labeled, starting from 0. You will go in and visit one room a day.\nInitially on day 0, you visit room 0. The order you visit the rooms for the coming days is determined by the following rules and a given 0-indexed array nextVisit of length n:\nReturn the label of the first day where you have been in all the rooms. It can be shown that such a day exists. Since the answer may be very large, return it modulo 109 + 7.\nExample 1:\nExample 2:\nExample 3:\nConstraints:",
  "examples": [
    {
      "example_num": 1,
      "example_text": "Input: nextVisit = [0,0]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\n- On day 0, you visit room 0. The total times you have been in room 0 is 1, which is odd.\n\u00a0 On the next day you will visit room nextVisit[0] = 0\n- On day 1, you visit room 0, The total times you have been in room 0 is 2, which is even.\n\u00a0 On the next day you will visit room (0 + 1) mod 2 = 1\n- On day 2, you visit room 1. This is the first day where you have been in all the rooms.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "example_num": 2,
      "example_text": "Input: nextVisit = [0,0,2]\nOutput: 6\nExplanation:\nYour room visiting order for each day is: [0,0,1,0,0,1,2,...].\nDay 6 is the first day where you have been in all the rooms.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "example_num": 3,
      "example_text": "Input: nextVisit = [0,1,2,0]\nOutput: 6\nExplanation:\nYour room visiting order for each day is: [0,0,1,1,2,2,3,...].\nDay 6 is the first day where you have been in all the rooms.",
      "images": []
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "n == nextVisit.length",
    "2 <= n <= 105",
    "0 <= nextVisit[i] <= i"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "The only way to get to room i+1 is when you are visiting room i and room i has been visited an even number of times.",
    "After visiting room i an odd number of times, you are required to visit room nextVisit[i] where nextVisit[i] <= i. It takes a fixed amount of days for you to come back from room nextVisit[i] to room i. Then, you have visited room i even number of times.nextVisit[i]",
    "Can you use Dynamic Programming to avoid recomputing the number of days it takes to visit room i from room nextVisit[i]?"
  ],
